  "basic_info_description": "Welcome to 2171 12th Avenue, a classic 1949 single-family home perfectly situated on the border of Golden Gate Heights and Forest Hills—two of San Francisco’s most desirable neighborhoods. This well-maintained residence captures the very best of West-side living with panoramic Pacific Ocean views from both the first and second floors, a quiet residential setting, and easy access to the friendly, walkable community of West Portal with its charming shops, cafés, and transit connections.  Key Property Details:\n•\t2 Bedrooms · 1 Bathroom · Approx. 1,100 sq. ft.\n•\tExpansive ocean and sunset views from nearly every room\n•\tReverse-floorplan design with the main living areas upstairs to maximize the views\n•\tSpacious lower level with laundry, storage, and excellent expansion potential -  within the existing footprint, the lower level can be easily reconfigured to add a third bedroom, second bath, office, and utility room — no external structural work required (homes on this side of 12th Ave with this completed upgrade have recently sold for over $1.8 million, demonstrating the strong value potential)\n•\tAttached tandem garage with off-street parking\n•\tLot size: approximately 2,996 sq. ft.\n•\tRecent updates: new water boiler, refreshed roof, and deck improvements for long-term reliability\n•\tEasy to maintain and low-cost to run, ideal for owner-occupiers or investors alike",
